For this new game, called Pokemon Depths, I want it to be like a basic roguelike where the title screen has a button called start run and when you begin a run, you get a choice of 3 starter Pokemon out of a larger pool (Kanto starters, Johto starters, …) 

The game has an overhead camera view just the Pokemon Rumble Run and you control your Pokemon to move throughout a procedurally generated 3d environment (like Pokemon Mystery Dungeon) 
- the more you explore, the more of the map gets unveiled on the top left (mini map) you can also click the menu bottom on the top right to pause which shows a more detailed view of the map) 

You can find items throughout the dungeon that boost your power
- What should some power ups be (one that evolves?, one that heals?, poke balls, item that reveals the floor plan, item that reveals all items and Pokemon locations on that floor, 

At the end of each floor is a Team Rocket Grunt on a space blocking the stairs upwards and when you bump into them, it begins a battle where your Pokemon automatically attack (basic Pokemon do 5 damage, Stage 1 Pokemon do 10, Stage 2 Pokemon do 15 damage, and legendaries do 20 damage per attack. Please take into account super effective types (no resistances or immunities). The team rocket grunts on floors 1-4 have randomized pokemon but always 1 Team Rocket themed Pokemon like Weezing or Arbok, etc. Make the floors get progressively more difficult but not too hard
- on the final floor is Giovanni and he always has Mewtwo on his team, 1 random legendary, 1 legendary bird, then 3 other random fully evolved Pokemon

